The application aims to improve the continuity, safety, and traceability of monitoring patients on oral anticoagulant therapy (OAT). Currently, dose delivery after PT/INR monitoring relies primarily on manual phone calls, internal records, and patient availability to answer, which can lead to delays, lack of confirmation of understanding, loss of traceability, and a risk of errors in treatment administration.

Furthermore, some patients do not fully understand the instructions before the monitoring, forget doses, or modify their treatment without medical authorization, which can affect the interpretation of PT/INR and hinder therapeutic adjustment.
The application will allow patients to check their monthly dose, next INR appointment, instructions before blood draws, nutritional information, and request contact with a nurse. For the clinical team, it will allow them to record, update, and track the delivery of instructions, reinforcing patient safety and monitoring of the OAT program.
